{"kind":"report","text":"Done. The wide docs artifact is retired and the merge guard is clear.\n\nRetirement event: ad272b0cab59e427565e43afe7c34c0ea69b6074, superseding 59d2b824d5aa811b5643195cf4e24fb353646643 at path `docs`, commit de274aac. Effective, authorized supersession, no successor published — per your condition I did not replace it with another broad `docs` artifact.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED BEFORE DOING IT, because a bare supersede of a still-cited artifact turns the docset gate red and I would rather not unblock one merge by breaking a gate.\n\nNothing cites it. I grepped the whole working tree for the full id and its abbreviation across Markdown, Go, JSON and YAML: no hits outside .git.\n\nThe pages it covered are already covered at the approved head: c726b428 at docs/reference/architecture.md and 48cdf8db at docs/reference/gs/merge.md, both live and not stale at ca5b378f0. So nothing is left uncovered by the retirement, and ox-builder's merge will carry those exact-path successors forward rather than needing a broad replacement.\n\nThe path is not emptied either — three older `docs` artifacts remain live-but-stale, so this is a retirement of one pointer rather than an abandonment of the area.\n\nONE FILING SLIP ON THE WAY, recorded since it is visible: my first supersede attempt was refused with \"causal reference does not resolve in this log\" because I built your request id by concatenating two abbreviations I had seen in different places — 1224dfa1 from the board listing and 51a7cb32 from your message — into an id that never existed. Those are the two ends of the same id. I resolved the real one from the projection and the second attempt landed. Nothing was written by the failed attempt.\n\nONE OBSERVATION FOR WHOEVER OWNS THE CONVENTION, not a request and not a reason to delay anything. Hours ago the correction ran the opposite way: ox-builder was told to retire file-level docs artifacts and publish a single `docs` one so the area keeps one maintained path, and I followed that same pattern when my merge sealed. Now the wide path is exactly what blocked a merge, because it sits outside the reviewed paths and belongs to another actor, and the remedy is exact-path successors.\n\nBoth rulings look right where they were made. But the convention pulls in two directions, and whoever publishes first constrains whoever merges next — a wide artifact is good for succession and bad for anyone else's reviewed-path bounds. It has now cost one round trip and will likely cost more. Worth someone writing down when an area wants one wide artifact and when it wants exact-path ones, so the next person is not choosing by coin flip.\n\n@ox-builder your merge should be unblocked; sorry it waited on me."}